          "name": "Vuetrex",
          "description": "Root scene container. Import Vuetrex and place the scene in its default slot.",
          "source": {
            "file": "dist_types/src/lib-components/root-api.d.ts",
            "offset": 510
          },
          "attributes": [
            {
              "name": "settings",
              "description": "Initial scene configuration. Read once at mount; remount with a new key to replace settings.",
              "default": "{}",
              "source": {
                "file": "dist_types/src/lib-components/root-api.d.ts",
                "offset": 657
              },
              "required": false,
              "value": {
                "kind": "expression",
                "type": {
                  "module": "@exceeder/vuetrex",
                  "name": "VxSettings"
                }
              },
              "description-sections": {
                "All settings": "| Name | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `color` | `number` | `0x555555` | Default node color. Zero currently falls back to the default. |\n| `backgroundColor` | `number` | `0x808080` | Solid scene background color. |\n| `mirrorOpacity` | `number` | `0.55` | Floor contribution over its reflection, clamped to 0–1. Lower values reveal more reflection; 1 skips the reflection pass. |\n| `floorColor` | `number` | `0x3f3f3f` | Floor texture color. When omitted, the reflection tint separately defaults to 0x777777. |\n| `floorFadeStart` | `number` | `undefined (disabled)` | World X/Z extent where floor fading begins. Set with floorFadeEnd; requires 0 <= start < end. Objects are unaffected. |\n| `floorFadeEnd` | `number` | `undefined (disabled)` | World X/Z extent where the floor matches the background. For example, start 20 and end 50 preserve the central 40-by-40 area. |\n| `highlightColor` | `number` | `0x4c7fb2` | Default interactive highlight color. Zero currently falls back to the default. |\n| `connectorColor` | `number` | `0xa0ffff` | Default connector color. |\n| `captionColor` | `number` | `0xffffff` | Floor caption and grid color. |\n| `lightColor1` | `number` | `0xccffff` | First directional light color. Zero currently falls back to the default. |\n| `lightColor2` | `number` | `0xffffff` | Second directional light color. Zero currently falls back to the default. |\n| `lightColor3` | `number` | `undefined` | Currently unused: the stage does not create a third light. |\n| `unit` | `number` | `1` | Base geometry unit in world units. Zero currently falls back to 1. |\n| `gap` | `number` | `1` | Default container spacing in world units. |\n| `fog` | `VxFogSettings` | `undefined (disabled)` | Linear camera-distance fog affecting the scene. Use floorFadeStart/floorFadeEnd to fade only the floor. |\n| `diagnostics` | `boolean \\| VxDiagnosticsSettings` | `false` | Enable all diagnostic overlays with true, or configure individual overlays. Omitted flags in an object are enabled. |\n| `floorGrid` | `boolean` | `true` | Draw the floor grid. |\n| `floorMirror` | `boolean` | `true` | Enable floor reflections. mirrorOpacity=1 also disables the reflection pass. |\n| `floorCaptions` | `boolean` | `true` | Draw node captions on the floor. |\n| `shadows` | `boolean` | `true` | Enable renderer shadow maps, shadow lights, and mesh shadow flags. |"
              }
            },
